A||||30||DXR_DAD||Business Ethics||||13||
Z||000000||DXR_DAD||04-21-2001||02:02 PM||||Another "drive by" from Terry at the Fiero Shop!! <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006765.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006765.html</A> <P>Props. go to Archie for not DISRESPECTING another members product and his post <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Rock, your a good guy. you gave no reply.<P>I know there are other menbers on the forum that do not respond to the Fiero Shop's post<BR>and I know why. I have talk with many of you and I know that others see whats going on.<P>But I got this one covered!! I do not need any help or for anyone to say anything. And I will not say who I have heard what from.<P>But Fiero Shop you need to take a good look at what's going on!!!!<P>Why is it that every time you post its to sell <B>a over priced item?</B> Never any help in the tech section from ya "The Fiero Shop" Then when you get mad cause nobody buys it. You drop the price, and drop in again.<P>Like I said you don't want to play this game.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||13
Z||000001||Loki||04-21-2001||02:17 PM||||Im not one to get involved in crap like this but here goes....DXR_DAD...Your a great Fiero guy.I needed some trim peices pretty bad cause I screwed mine up. You sent em no charge.. Very much impressed me (Hope to help you out in the future).. The Fiero shop wanted to charge me like $45 for 3 gauge trim pieces. I know these are not made anymore, but for $45 I can make copies outta some lexen (hmmmm idea????)  I like alot of the stuff the Fiero shop sells, but its way outta my leage money wise. Ive seen very similar hood scoops for like $300 less and looks easier to install.  Ive seen alot of bickering by people in the last few months and will it ever end? no....Its a fact of life  people dont like people.  But DXR_DAD  you got my vote...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||04-21-2001||02:22 PM||||ok Bill, you are beginning to get to me with your little games here -- "drive-by" - maybe in your neighborhood that is what it's called..........there is nothing wrong with that post unless it was to make others aware that there are alternatives (something you fail to do) -- this is a big world and one in which we should be able to co-exist. You, however, seem to delight in digging up posts and trying to make something out of them - as for a product being overpriced - that is one of opinion -- price is determined by labor hours and material costs plus overheads and a fair profit margin to determine a selling price. What may be overpriced to you may not be to someone else.........after all, everyone knows what their product is worth - If others feel theirs is worth less than so be it.......who am I to say that it is or isn't.........<P>"I know there are other menbers on the forum that do not respond to the Fiero Shop's post<BR>and I know why. I have talk with many of you and I know that others see whats going on." -- now, another inference that something is going on..............you really do delight in this, don't you?<P>As for "fieroshop" - get it straight - I, myself, post as tgowens and have made many a post in the technical section. (I don't see you there often though so you might not want to throw those stones........) as for "fieroshop" maybe George has a reason for not posting more or in a certain section -- I suggest that you address that with him rather than me.........for what it's worth to you (or anyone else who may read this) I simply came out here to help in the shop and am not legally or financially responsible for the operations of this shop -- I do have the right to post here and to say what I feel too (as well as you do) but have never taken a shot at you in a degeratory manner and you know it -- Business Ethics?? I know what they are and in fact have taught a course in it when I was a sales trainer -- but, Business Ethics prevent me from jumping down and equalizing some of the statements that you have made. I choose not to and that is because of who I am and what I am all about.<P>And, you are entirely correct, I don't want to play this game - I will leave the games to you and those of your choice, as for me, I desire to act responsibly and professionally and in a business manner.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||04-21-2001||02:54 PM||||Quote:<BR>{You, however, seem to delight in digging up posts and trying to make something out of them} <P>Terry you seemed to want to make something out of my "Bay Area Shops" topic. You made something out of it that I DID NOT SAY!!!<BR>Again I did not say nor did I mean that these were the only shops that work on fieros<BR>in the bay area!! How would I know about ALL the shops in the bay area. San Francisco is a big place??? <B>Think about it Terry</B><BR>what you said makes no sence!<P>Maybe you should read Stimpy's reply.<P>And because your the Fieroshop who works on fieros ONLY! I would think you would be more help in the tech section!! I on the other hand do not work for a Fiero Only shop and do not have a Fiero Only shop that sell Fiero parts.<P><BR>Thank you Loki  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> anytime I can be of help let me know.<P><BR>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 04-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||04-21-2001||03:05 PM||||you are entirely correct Bill, you did not say those were the only shops (re-read my post again - you <I>implied</I> it by the way your post was worded.<P>"How would I know about ALL the shops in the bay area. San Francisco is a big place??? Think about it Terry what you said makes no sence!" -  here you are implying that you simply didn't realize that the Fiero Shop was in the Bay Area -- Bill, your omission was blatant and obvious and <I>that</I> makes no sen<B>s</B>e-- all I did was make a reference to the fact that we are here and you failed to mention us along with other shops in the Bay Area and for you to say that you don't know about the Fiero Shop is totally ludicrous.......you did attend a Poker Run which was partly sponsored by the Fiero Shop last March, didn't you?<P>You need to separate me from George and the Fiero Shop -- if you are intending to take shots at me personally I will take it off of this forum - this is not the place to air a personal grievance........address it with the individual involved.<P>I will say nothing further on this topic.......<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 04-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||04-21-2001||03:23 PM||||Here are the exact words in my post:<P>{There was a post a while back about repair shops that will work on Fieros, and where to find good shops. So this is a day in the live of a fiero owner and a few good So. San Francisco shops. For all you Bay Area members.  This is my buddys shop}<P><B>Notice I said: A few...good So. San Francisco shops</B><P>NOT the ONLY<P>And yes my remarks are to THE FIERO SHOP!<BR>and that means Terry and George ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||04-21-2001||03:44 PM||||All I am going to say is that I have dealt with both George and DXR_DAD. The dealings with both have been good. I have no complaints with either.<BR>As for the hood vent issue, The norm around the forum is that when someone posts a thread looking for a particular item usually those that have a simular item also post also. Is it "ethical"? I really don't know. But it does show alternate things that are available. Personally, if someone inquire's about an particular mod, those that make them should post option's. However, If those that make the mod's post, it should only be their item. This is just my opinion, and I hope that we do not get into a "war" over the difference's.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||04-21-2001||04:35 PM||||Guess it's time to put my 2c in. <B>Personally</B>, I see nothing wrong with a vendor throwing in his products in a thread. Nobody is forced to buy anything and the more alternatives are given, the better. In fact, one of the reasons this forum has become so succesful (again IMO) is because both Fiero-<B>owners</B> and -<B>vendors</B> hang out here. Maybe some vendors are more expensive than others but that's how a free market works. Besides, take the most expensive price you can find for an item, multiply that by four, and you have a pretty good idea how much it would cost here in Holland.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>But that's my personal opinion. I don't make the rules here - I've said it many times before: the members do. I just try to enforce them.<P>One thing that does concern me a bit is that the forum is used more and more to fight out personal vendettas. Before you post such a message, please realize one thing: that probably 80% of the members here simply are not interested in what you have to say, or have no clue <B>what</B> your point is. If you <B>must</B> react to a posting in another thread, please do so in <B>that</B> thread. For instance, on the topic of this thread alone, there are three other threads (that I know of).<P>In short, do what you will - it's still your forum. But keep it a fun and interesting place. I just read the first negative comment about this forum somewhere else. That was scary. And a shame.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||04-21-2001||04:40 PM||||Hmm.  I too had questioned the price of the hood scoops and was attacked by tgowens for not being a "do-er" just a "talker".  That thread has mysteriously disappeared from the forum however. But basically I responded to tgowens question about why a bunch of people were interested back then now all the sudden not too many people are, and I told him the truth about the price and how I too have talked to about 5 or 6 forum guys on AOL IM and they all said the same thing. <P> So I'm not trying to start anything, and I wasnt going to respond at first until I couldn't find my original reply to tgowens about the hood vents.  <P>disclaimer: I could be wrong about this disappearing thread but I looked for 30 minutes in every forum and I couldn't find it.  <BR>||||reg||11
Z||000009||Cliff Pennock||04-21-2001||05:09 PM||||I hardly ever delete threads. I close them every now and then, but try not to delete them (unless I feel I can prevent some heavy flamewar by doing so). I really don't mind people questioning vendors, or vendors throwing in their products. Just keep it clean and civilized. That's all I ask. I don't want to say this all too often but I spend a lot of time and money on this forum and as you all know I don't make a single buck out of it. That's fine with me but please realize that every post you make means more resources are taken, more bandwidth is used and more work needs to be done by me to keep it all up and running. I'd rather not see all the work I've put into this go to waste because of all the (unnecessary) flamewars.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||tgowens||04-21-2001||05:15 PM||||Folks, as I have said, price is a relative term - it relates to the elements which make up the product. I do not set the prices for Fiero Shop products nor do I manufacture them. I simply state what is presented to me and "pass the word along".<P>And - I do not "attack" anyone without first being provoked. That is not my nature - never has been and never will be.<P>As I have said before - this is a country where innovation is imminent, products and designs are brought to the marketplace every day and a price is established by the manufacturer for what he feels is fair for the product. No business can afford to give anything away or discount to the point of no profit if they expect to keep the doors open and further serve the community.<P>And, I have said it before and I will once again - I have no legal or financial responsibility for Fiero Shop or its manufactured products. I will stand behind <B>my</B> work (both auto and web design) as I always have. Customer satisfaction means a lot to me and I have been in business in various positions for over thirty years now dealing with the public. - so, my point is: If there is a complaint with the shop, address it with the owner rather than expecting me to relay messages or undermine him -- that is not my position in being here. <P>I act on shop business when it is appropriate and with the authority of the shop owner, otherwise I act of my own accord and live up to my own statements and actions.<P>As far as this Forum goes, I respect the wishes and direction of our esteemed moderator, Cliff Pennock. I agree with his post on this subject and with that - I leave this post.........<P>Now, can we put this to rest and get back to the fun???||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||04-21-2001||05:39 PM||||Cliff, I'm not sure what happened to the thread to be honest with you.  I could be just looking under the wrong name, like you know how things with certain topics tend to change to other topics in the middle of the thread.  <P>But the Fiero shop has helped me out before so I can't come down on them too much.  I was just a little disgruntled when I couldn't find my original "dissenting statement" about the hood vents. <P>like tgowens said, lets get back to the fun...||||reg||1
Z||000012||fieroshop||04-21-2001||05:52 PM||||In all sincerity I do not post a lot for the reason I don't have the time to.<BR>I don't post to the tech side for the reason that when somebody asks a question there are several answers. Some good and some bad. I don't want to contradict those that are bad and make them look bad. So I have a toll free number that people call me and I am glad to give them advice over the phone. I have had a lot of calls asking for advice as some of you who have called know. <BR>Bill before you start judging people because they don't post as per your desires I suggest you look in the mirror and ask yourself why am I doing this as I don't post in the tech section at all?<P>------------------<BR> <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroshop_sig_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 04-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Slick781||04-21-2001||07:48 PM||||hey, does anybody know where i can perhaps buy some good hood scoops?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'm just kidding  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>People need to lighten up in this place.  When you start building a big forum like this, there will be many people you consider dumb@%#es, but its not like we have to see these people, we just might spend 3 seconds to read an annoying post by them... who cares?  WHen i come across these, I just laugh and call my dad in here to read them with me, and laugh about it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But it doesnt bother me to the point that I feel the need to say anything to the person.<P>Heck, sometimes when i post, since I'm so inexperienced with car stuff, but hope become MORE experienced, I think to myself... "man, these people are gonna think I'm a friggin moron"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But then i post anyways, cuz in this great place, even the morons get replies to thier questions  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I just ask that everyone be patient with me, because since we have relatively no money to rebuild our 85 GT, my questions are always "how can i do this cheaply?"  questions, when might tend to annoy some of the better off folks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Lighten up ppl, its just the internet.<P>David||||reg||1
Z||000014||Galen||04-21-2001||09:26 PM||||ummm.. uh huh, okie. I dont get it. I simply dont get it. Could someone explain to me, why, people insist on talkin to me?<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Archie||04-21-2001||09:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DXR_DAD:<BR><B><BR>Props. go to Archie for not DISRESPECTING another members product and his post  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ok, I've been home for an hour or so and I've been Trying to figure out what's up with this thread. First I asked myself what "Props." means? Like is "Props." good or bad? If it's good Then THANKS DXR. If it's bad what did I do wrong? Then I asked myself what I did to be included in this?<P>Then I go to the link to the other thread, then the link that took me to this site <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/extractorinstall.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/extractorinstall.htm</A>  this is a cool scoop.... a very cool scoop..... Then the light goes on, I understand, I figured it out "Props." is good!  <P>Thanks DXR_DAD.<P>I must add my opinion on this whole thread.<P>I personally think that if someone wants to promote an item, they should do it in their own thread. I think others with similar products should have enough self respect to refrain from just plastering up links to promote their own stuff on someone elses' thread. Especially when their own stuff is already being promoted in the same forum.<P>As for the vents in the above thread, why should I get upset about them? They look great!!!!, I didn't even know they existed. I'm glad someone started that thread. I can't speak for the quality or easy of installation.  But I can tell you that if someone sent me a set, I'd slap them on my next car ASAP and be happy to brag about them.<P>It is obvious that these vents are original designs and not copies of anything I've seen before. <P>Whoever designed these should be proud, as I'm proud of our "Warber" hoods. <P>Ok guys...... You can go back to the Flame Wars.<P>Archie<P>P.S., Please donot take this post as an endorsement of a product I have not inspected &/or used myself. <P>Please DO take this post as a statement of respect for those who would market items of original & unique design.<P>Thanks<P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||GT Bastard||04-21-2001||10:22 PM||||I think I've mentioned this once or twice, but I enjoy reading and participating in flame wars.  It really spices up the forum.  Just picturing some dude all pi$$ed-off over something that was posted online is funny to imagine. Like Slick said, it's just the internet. ||||reg||1
Z||000017||noyb||04-21-2001||11:15 PM||||Personally, I think you boys ought to meet at the nearest public restroom, go in, unzip, compare sizes, and let the smaller man tuck and run.  ||||reg||1
Z||000018||zeusrekning||04-22-2001||10:34 PM||||As someone who doesn't make any products do sell here. If I were to want a hood scoop, engine kit, tires. rebody, etc.,  etc. I would want to see every possible product there is for what ever i was looking for. As Archie said , he had never seen those hood scoops, now he has and likes them.So that was good.<P>And I think flame wars are good occasionally.  But, only when it is some ricer or MR2 guy (if there is a difference) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> comes in here running his mouth.<P>It makes us look bad when two of our senior members flame each other. If have heard great things about fiero shop, i think prices are high but they do have a lot of stuff and have to make a profit to keep it up. And i have heard great things about DRXdad and seen the hood scoop on turbo86se's car  (liked it) <P><BR>Lets just bash rice again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ??<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||AusFiero||04-23-2001||05:38 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Besides, take the most expensive price you can find for an item, multiply that by four, and you have a pretty good idea how much it would cost here in Holland.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I can relate to that Cliff...these guys don't know expensive, half their luck. We have to triple a USA price to have it in our hands in Australia. Your tax rates must be worse than ours.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||tgowens||04-23-2001||11:29 AM||||What I find the most interesting about threads like this one is, the person who starts them stirs it up a little, sits back and watches others fall into the pot, and then silently slips out the door while everyone else is left boiling.........kinda makes ya wonder what the original intent was, doesn't it?||||reg||1
Z||000021||DXR_DAD||04-23-2001||12:09 PM||||Another "Drive BY" Good one Terry!!!!<P>What's funny is your statement in another post,  Remember this?<P><BR>Quote<BR>I respected Cliff's wishes that threads like this not exist but others feel the need to make their remarks and keep it at the top......it's very simple.........let it die by not making any replies to this thread and it sill simply fade away........<P>enough said..........<BR>End Quote<BR>here take a look!! <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006981.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006981.html</A> <P>Maybe you should read it and take your own advice!!!!! <P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 04-23-2001).]||||reg||10
