Z||000023||tgowens||04-23-2001||01:19 PM||||Bill, I will say this here and only once - you start these things and then want to "play games" - personally, I am tired of it and I think others here are too - as for "drive bys" - you are so hypocritical - you do the very same thing and then want to make an issue when I do it -- there are a lot of things I could say here but I won't because I simply don't feel that I can get down to your level - not now, not ever -- take the games and play them with someone else because I am not interested in anything you have to do or say.<P>Now, run along and play, ok?||||reg||1
Z||000024||Oreif||04-23-2001||02:42 PM||||The below was to be a reply to the "Disclaimer" thread but was locked while I typed.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>I, Terry Owens, have no legal nor financial responsibility for Fiero Shop of Richmond, CA. Any and all decisions for the operation of Fiero Shop are the sole responsibility of its owner. The Fiero Shop of Richmond, CA may be reached toll free at 866-534-8486.<P>----------<P>Now, let it be known that whatever agreements I may have with George Miller are my own and for whatever reasons I choose. I was asked last July to come out here to help George move the shop and its contents to a new location and to assist in the maintenance and repair of Fieros. This I did of my own volition. <I>I do not make financial or operational decisions concerning the operation of the shop, repair of vehicles or sale of parts. </I> I am not responsible for the Fiero Shop web site nor its content. <P>----------<P>Terry Owens<BR>4/23/2001</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Terry, I don't want to get into this disagreement that seems to be growing, But Just doing a quick search thru the different sections of the forum, I have found numerous posts by you. These posts for parts or service are always ended with "Call <B> US </B> at the shop." That implies that George and you are working together at the Fiero Shop. I as well as many others would assume by these posts that the above is true.<BR>I don't have a problem recommending a business or vendor who I have dealt with, But usually I refer to them as a seperate business. You always seem to imply that George and you <B>ARE </B> "The Fiero Shop". <BR>I think that it is part of the confusion that has had you associated with any dissatisfied customers. <BR>Like I said before, I have talked with George and have bought parts thru him. There was no complaints. If George had a part I was looking for at a reasonable price to me, I'd buy without any concerns. <BR>Please don't take this as slam against you, This is just a viewpoint that others may also assume by the way your past posts have shown.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000025||FieroMike||04-23-2001||02:56 PM||||If it's too expensive, don't buy it.  That about sums it up for me.  I don't understand how an over-priced item could make you so mad, what happens when there is a real problem?||||reg||4
Z||000026||tgowens||04-23-2001||02:59 PM||||Dave, I understand what you are saying -- the term "us" is a collective term and as such I can understand people <I>assuming</I> that George and I work together. When, in fact, we <I>do</I> work together - the difference being that I work <B>with</B> George and not <B>for</B> him. I <I>have</I> made numerous posts in an attempt to help him build his business and do so by his direction. Prices quoted, services offered, etc are set by him and I post those at his direction and with his authority.<P>I can understand the confusion and perhaps it would be better, in order to eliminate the confusion, if I did not post here at all. I have made my position known several times here and have made the same position known to others through email and via phone.<P>I made the disclaimer simply to dispel any ideas that I am somehow responsible for tha actions or statements of another. I, however, will stand behind any statements or actions I make and I think that anyone who knows me knows that.<P>There are just a few people who seem to not be able to understand the association I have here, even though I have stated it repeatedly, and for any misunderstandings, I am truly sorry. There are also others who, for whatever reason, feel the need to create more of a mess than need be by posting remarks and grievances here that should be directed by email or by phone to the responsible party.<P>I do want to thank Cliff for his jurisdiction and actions on these many postings. Cliff runs a clean forum here and I have enjoyed participating in it however, it just isn't fun any more.<P>I apologize for any misunderstandings but I will not apologize for my having been put on the defensive by the statements of others. If thereis a complaint with the operations of the Fiero Shop, address that with the shop owner rather than attempting to undermine my integrity and credibility.||||reg||1
